gecko (0.3.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.3.3: a desktop window whose page was killed
    (by the out-of-memory killer or a crash) reloads it instead of
    freezing on its last frame. gecko url and gecko open no longer report
    the default port from a daemon they have just started.

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.3.2: Codex and OpenCode have their own status,
    so a paused, stopped or waiting agent no longer shows as working. On
    Android, a long-press on a machine with the keyboard up opens its
    menu. gecko share off also cuts off a browser still connecting.

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.3.1: Make anchor (protocol 11: any machine in
    the sidebar can become the anchor, remembered across launches, relay
    anchoring on by default), gecko upgrade restarts into the binary it
    installed, and make install is atomic and links other gecko copies
    under home to the new one. Closed tabs no longer come back, and a
    phone keeps its terminal size when a window elsewhere reconnects.

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.3.0: see-through windows on macOS and Windows
    (no vibrancy or acrylic material), the anchor (protocol 10: the Gecko
    you connect to manages every other machine, and relay peers get a
    scope the server enforces), and the web app on phones (install, a
    Settings sheet, pinch changes the text size, tabs switch on every tap).

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.2.2: light themes readable on desktop (WebGL
    blending fix, minimum contrast, AA chrome on every theme, the "gecko"
    theme follows the OS), and a key bar that fits 360 dp phones, with
    drawn arrow keys, Shift+Tab and Claude Code's mode symbols.

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.2.1: Termux is one of This phone's machines in
    the Android app, machines can be added by their Gecko link, Claude Code
    in Termux on arm64, share links pick the right address, and the Android
    app's Termux setup no longer writes the link token to logcat.

 -- Gecko contributors <gecko@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

gecko (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.2.0: Android and iOS apps, desktop apps, Linux
    packages, static-PIE Linux binaries for Termux, sticky sessions through
    a relay, WebTransport and fast reconnects, start at login.

